      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T20:23:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is useful coverage: as far as I can see, no other P3S test checks argv and environment contents after a 4KB exec.\n\nI\u0027m worried it passes without P3S on 4KB kernels, though. `main()` re-execs with `exec_compat()` without checking that it starts as a native 16KB process. On a 4KB arm64 kernel, or on x86_64, `personality()` takes `ADDR_PAGE_SIZE_4KB` like any other bit, so the child has 4KB pages and the bit set, `p3s_require_compat()` lets it through, and both checks pass.\n\nCould `main()` skip in that case, as `p3s_compat_main()` does before its re-exec? For example, before setting the variables:\n\n```\n\tif (getpagesize() !\u003d NATIVE_PAGE_SIZE) {\n\t\tksft_print_header();\n\t\tksft_exit_skip(\"native exec does not use 16K pages\\n\");\n\t}\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "93843185e3000271fa3d54b41bb89deff49164dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
